3. Functional & Technical Requirements
3.1 Query Optimization Engine
Objective

Improve execution performance for complex dashboards.

Problem

Current execution flow likely:

Load full dataset

Apply transformations

Apply filters

Apply joins

Compute measures

Return aggregated result

This becomes slow as datasets grow.

Requirements

System must introduce a query planner that:

Analyzes requested fields.

Determines minimal required columns.

Applies filters early (predicate pushdown).

Applies joins only if necessary.

Applies grouping before expensive operations.

Query Execution Flow (Optimized)

Identify required tables.

Identify required columns.

Push filters to earliest stage.

Apply joins (if multi-table).

Apply grouping.

Compute measures.

Apply sorting & chart-level filters.

Acceptance Criteria

Dashboard render time improves vs baseline.

No unnecessary full-table scans.

Unused columns not processed.

Performance measurable improvement (≥30%).

3.2 Aggregation Caching Layer
Objective

Avoid recomputing identical aggregations.

Requirements

Implement caching for:

Filtered datasets

Aggregated group results

Computed measures

Cache key must consider:

Dataset version

Active filters

Drill state

Measure definitions

Grouping dimensions

Cache Structure Example
{
  "cacheKey": "dataset1|region=East|measure=SUM(Revenue)|group=Month",
  "result": {}
}
Rules

Cache invalidates when:

Dataset updated

Transformation changes

Measure modified

TTL optional.

Cache must not leak memory.

Acceptance Criteria

Repeated chart loads return instantly.

Cache invalidates correctly.

No stale data displayed.

Memory usage controlled.

3.3 Large Dataset Handling
Objective

Support datasets beyond 50k rows (target: 1M+ rows).

Requirements
1. Columnar Data Storage

Store datasets in columnar format internally:

Instead of:

[ {row1}, {row2} ]

Use:

{
  "Revenue": [],
  "Region": [],
  "Date": []
}

Improves aggregation speed.

2. Virtualized Data Preview

Render rows virtually.

Never render full dataset in DOM.

Load chunks (e.g., 100 rows per batch).

3. Server-Side Aggregation

For large datasets:

Move heavy aggregations to backend.

Frontend only renders result set.

4. Data Chunking

Process dataset in chunks.

Avoid blocking main thread.

Acceptance Criteria

500k rows manageable.

No UI freeze.

Preview loads smoothly.

Aggregation time remains acceptable (<1s typical case).

3.4 Incremental Data Refresh
Objective

Avoid full recompute when only part of dataset changes.

Requirements

System must support:

Dataset versioning.

Incremental refresh logic:

Only process new rows.

Scheduled refresh (optional backend job).

Dataset Version Structure
{
  "datasetId": "Sales",
  "version": 3,
  "lastUpdated": "2026-03-01"
}
Acceptance Criteria

Updating dataset does not reset entire model unnecessarily.

Cached aggregations update correctly.

Dashboard remains functional during refresh.

3.5 Background Processing Architecture
Objective

Prevent UI blocking during heavy operations.

Requirements

Heavy tasks must run:

In Web Worker (frontend), OR

In backend worker process

Tasks to offload:

Clustering

Forecasting

Large joins

Complex aggregations

Cache rebuilding

Requirements

Non-blocking UI.

Show loading indicators.

Cancel running computation if user changes filter.

Acceptance Criteria

UI responsive during heavy tasks.

No browser freeze.

Cancelling operation works correctly.

3.6 Live Database Connectors
Objective

Enable direct database connectivity (without file upload).

Supported Connectors (Minimum)

MySQL

PostgreSQL

SQL Server

Functional Requirements

User must be able to:

Add new connection.

Enter credentials securely.

Select database.

Select table.

Preview data.

Enable live mode OR import mode.

Security Requirements

Credentials encrypted.

No raw query execution from user input.

Parameterized queries only.

Query sandboxing required.

Query Execution Modes
Import Mode

Load data once.

Use internal engine.

Live Mode

Query database directly for aggregations.

Acceptance Criteria

Successful DB connection.

Live chart renders correctly.

Filters translate to SQL WHERE.

No SQL injection possible.

